Price of Freedom Wraith, Omnitron-U, Darkwatch Mr. Fixer, and Unity Classic vs The Chairman at Pike Industrial Complex

&nbsp;

Whoo boy, this one was a doozy. &nbsp;I managed to mint it, but barely. &nbsp;Everyone was in single digits by the end of it.

&nbsp;

[table][row color=#FFFFFF][color=#FFFFFF]The first play is a Broker, followed by both Prison Breaks, then The Muscle. &nbsp;Operative pulls out Crooked Cop, The Contract, then The Fence. &nbsp;All five Underbosses WILL be in play before you can flip the Chairman. &nbsp;At that point, it&#39;s just damage mitigation. &nbsp;I very quickly realized that I needed to solve this with a Hasty Augmented Defensive Blast, so I was kicking myself when I didn&#39;t grab a Plating with Omnitron&#39;s Technological Advancement. &nbsp;Wraith and Fixer are purely on Thug control, and are you main nethod for clearing Underbosses with Omnitron-U&#39;s base power, which you should be spamming every turn. &nbsp;Pike is actually pretty helpful, giving a Chemical Explosion right off the bat, then a Trisolvent Cooling Vat, a Biomemetic Plasma Vat, a Rat, then another Explosion, and another Plasma Vat. &nbsp;Wraith gets her Grappling Hooks early, so take advantage of them to clear the vats before they cause too much damage. &nbsp;Fixer should be detonating Omnitron-U&#39;s components each turn to get that free damage in, and Unity should be making her Bots. &nbsp;Fixer has Overdrive and two Salvage Yards in his first draws, so you can dish out a LOT of damage rather quickly. &nbsp;Unity starts with a Supply Crate and Cryo Bot, and will draw a Platform Bot and Raptor Bot early. &nbsp;Her next bot isn&#39;t until Stealth Bot, however. &nbsp;Cryo Bot is a champ, though.[/color][/row][/table]

&nbsp;

Sorry about the blatant spoilers, those who&#39;ve already seen it. &nbsp;I&#39;ve got them edited out now. &nbsp;You can highlight if you want to read them.
